# Enum array arguments

pgx has no encode plan for a slice of a named string enum (`[]Status`) into an unregistered Postgres enum array. Passing that slice fails before the query runs.

Implement `database/sql/driver.Valuer` on a named slice type. `Value` returns the Postgres array literal. Keep `Scan` and `Value` off the singular enum; a single value encodes through `MarshalText`.

Do not loop the values into `[]string` at the call site.

Name the slice the plural of the enum when that name is free. When a `Statuses()` helper already uses it, name the slice `StatusValues`.

```go
// GOOD — the slice type implements driver.Valuer
type StatusValues []Status

var (
	_ driver.Valuer = StatusValues(nil)
)

func (values StatusValues) Value() (driver.Value, error) {
	if len(values) == 0 {
		return nil, nil
	}

	var result strings.Builder
	result.WriteString("{")

	for i, value := range values {
		if i > 0 {
			result.WriteString(",")
		}

		fmt.Fprintf(&result, "%q", value.String())
	}

	result.WriteString("}")

	return result.String(), nil
}

"statuses": StatusValues{StatusRejected, StatusRevoked},

// BAD — no encode plan for []Status
"statuses": []Status{StatusRejected, StatusRevoked},

// BAD — converts to []string instead of implementing driver.Valuer
encoded := make([]string, len(values))
for i, value := range values {
	encoded[i] = value.String()
}
```

An empty slice returns `nil`, so `WHEN @statuses::status[] IS NOT NULL` leaves the filter off. The SQL still casts the parameter: `status = ANY(@statuses::status[])`.

See [`contrib/claude/coredata.md`](../../contrib/claude/coredata.md) (Enum arrays).
